# Things not packed into the image at build time (works like .gitignore, but for Docker).
# Background: ADD . /app in the Dockerfile puts the whole api-service folder into the image;
#       the items below are caches or system files made automatically when running locally; the image doesn't need them, so leaving them out keeps the image cleaner and the build faster.
# Note: during development docker-compose mounts the code into the container; mounts aren't affected by this file, it only affects the built image.

# Caches Python makes automatically when running
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Caches left over after running pytest and ruff
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The local virtual env (the image has its own /.venv; the one on the Mac can't be used)
.venv/

# Files the Mac makes automatically
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Safety net: if someone ever puts a key in this folder, it still won't be packed into the image
secrets/
*service-account*.json

# Additional local configuration and editable-package metadata
.env
.env.*
*.egg-info/
